---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBasePath } from '../lib/site-paths';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Learn about Terapixel Games and the browser games you can play here."
>
  <div class="shell stack">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1 class="page-title">About Terapixel Games</h1>
      <p class="page-copy">
        Terapixel Games makes small arcade, puzzle, racing, action, and card games you can play in a modern browser.
        The goal is simple: quick games that are easy to start and satisfying to replay.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="content-grid" aria-label="Studio principles">
      <article class="glass-panel text-panel">
        <h2>What We Make</h2>
        <p>
          We make lightweight web games with immediate controls, readable goals, and short repeatable runs. The current
          lineup includes arcade movement, color-matching puzzles, toy-scale racing, reflex challenges, and fast card games.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="glass-panel text-panel">
        <h2>What Shows Up Here</h2>
        <p>
          The Games page focuses on titles you can play now. If a game is still being worked on, it stays out of the
          main library until it is ready to try.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="glass-panel text-panel">
        <h2>What Players Can Expect</h2>
        <p>
          Every game page should tell you the goal, the basic controls, and a few useful tips. If something breaks, the
          Support and Contact pages give you a direct way to report it.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="glass-panel text-panel">
        <h2>No Download Runaround</h2>
        <p>
          Games are meant to run in the browser. We do not ask players to chase fake download buttons or dig through a
          long signup flow before finding something to play.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="glass-panel text-panel">
        <h2>Kept Playable</h2>
        <p>
          We check the public pages for broken links, confusing labels, and stale game information. When a game changes,
          its page should change with it.
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="glass-panel text-panel" aria-labelledby="contact-heading">
      <h2 id="contact-heading">Contact the Studio</h2>
      <p>
        For gameplay reports, privacy questions, or partnership inquiries, email
        <a href="mailto:support@terapixel.games">support@terapixel.games</a> or use the
        <a href={withBasePath('/support')}>Support page</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
